<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="obsidian-fragments-valor-points">Obsidian Fragments &amp; Valor Points for Holy Paladin Healer in Phase 4</h3>With Phase 4, Cataclysm Classic has a new dungeon difficulty added: Protocol Twilight. Completing these instances will reward you with <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3281/obsidian-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Obsidian Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_stone_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Obsidian Fragment</span></span></a>, which can be traded in for <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5892/dragon-soul">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Dragon Soul</span></a> LFR gear and tier 12 Normal mode items, as well several other items. In contrast to Protocol Inferno Dungeons, the end bosses of Protocol Twilight Dungeons drop <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5892/dragon-soul">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Dragon Soul</span></a> LFR gear in addition to the new currency, making them a much quicker method of gearing up. Other than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=78485/maw-of-the-dragonlord">
<img alt="Maw of the Dragonlord" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_1h_deathwingraiddw_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Maw of the Dragonlord</span></a>, the table below should be considered only a loose priority, and your focus should be on upgrading your lowest item level pieces. Use the <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> you gain on <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77096/woundlicker-cover">
<img alt="Woundlicker Cover" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cape_deathwingraid_d_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Woundlicker Cover</span></a> followed by <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77109/band-of-reconstruction">
<img alt="Band of Reconstruction" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_ring_generic_1.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Band of Reconstruction</span></a>,  and then to fill in any remaining gaps in your gear.<br/>
<br/>
